  clock: 4  # 32a0
  nonce: 32a0  # 32a0
  message: "Fixed in PR #1938 (dev bf610aad12). scan_content now runs gitleaks with cwd= an empty tmp_artifact_dir of its own and --report-path - (stdout), instead of the inherited cwd and /dev/stdout. Filed repro re-run on merged dev bf610aad12 through the production scan_content: from a cwd holding a .gitleaks.toml allowlist for ghp_ tokens, a GitHub PAT now gives 1 finding (github-pat), where dev 4892851370 gave 0; strace of that run records 0 operations on /dev/stdout (before: openat O_CREAT|O_TRUNC + two unlinkat). strace of a full `hypergumbo sketch` on a repo holding .gitleaks.toml and .gitleaksignore: gitleaks' threads look for both only in the scratch dir (ENOENT); argv carries --report-path -. Tests: TestScanRunsInADirectoryOfItsOwn (report on -, never /dev/stdout; cwd not the caller's, empty at launch, removed after) and a real-binary test (cwd .gitleaks.toml does not hide an AWS key); mutation-checked both ways. Operator opt-in kept: gitleaks' GITLEAKS_CONFIG / GITLEAKS_CONFIG_TOML env vars are still honoured (documented in README and the gitleaks.py comment). check-self-claims: 18 claims unchanged. README untrusted-repository bullet, claims text and SECURITY.md updated. NOT observed: the root-only unlink succeeding; it is no longer attempted, so the case is moot."  # 32a0
